{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ER7cb4Y4qZEzQwLbS3LHg6","type":"tool_result","content":"?? docs/reviews/wi-927/005-ADJUDICATE-65a3405.md\n?? docs/reviews/wi-927/005-ADJUDICATE-65a3405.md.requested\n65a340522 WI-927: the checkpoint's reconcile: LLR-322, LLR-300 and TC-345 state the settled fix; the Trust section reads the ratchet line and corrects the offer's count; decision D-010\n4b20a7bc3 WI-927: the round-2 MINOR fix: a failed install names its fix, a NUL stdin is no terminal on Windows, and the PowerShell offers print the guard's text; LLR-322's back-links; decision D-009\n0c41237c9 WI-927: counted round 2, filed (Sol CHANGES-REQUESTED 1 MINOR; Opus CHANGES-REQUESTED 5 MINOR); decision D-008\n9bbcfb351 WI-927: fix round 1: a JSON null reads occupied, the consent question shows at a POSIX terminal, and the pseudo-terminal tests answer no; decision D-007\nbrief = combined\nkinds = amendment\noutcome = pending\n124:human_approval_through = \"DevStg-Boundary\"\nSR-229 Coordinator claim admission respects a blackout pause\r\n REQ: Where a blackout window is armed, the delivered work-item admission shall refuse a new claim inside that window on every route at any context-guard dial; outside a blackout window, where the declared coordinator context guard is enabled, it admits a coordinator claim only from the current lease holder while that holder's context drain is not latched, the drain latching once the holder's context occupancy reaches the declared threshold and holding across compaction and resume until the owner records a clear or a release, the holder records a hand-back naming its handoff, or a relaunched successor takes the lease.\r\n AC: Inside an armed blackout window, every claim route, including the unattended dispatcher, refuses a new claim naming the window end at any dial; outside it, with the guard off, admission proceeds without reading or writing guard state; with it on, the holder below the threshold may claim, while a claim with no lease held, a claim from another session or from a caller naming no session, and a claim from a holder at or above the threshold each refuse, naming the recovery action. The unattended dispatcher's own admission remains available without consulting this guard. Occupancy counts the newest valid post-compaction usage on the live branch, including cached input, and unknown usage is not zero. A latched drain survives a lower reading, compaction and resume, and ends only when the owner records a clear or a release, the holder records a hand-back naming its handoff, or a relaunched successor takes the lease. With the guard off, a hand-back reads and writes no guard state. Only the holder may record a hand-back, which names a handoff carrying a session prompt; another or unnamed caller is refused, naming the owner's release, whatever handoff it names; the holder's promptless handoff or own pending relaunch request is refused; a relaunch request left by a previous holder does not block the hand-back; and a subsequent session may take the freed lease.\r\n status Approved\r\n\r\nSR-237 Blackout pauses new model work and resumes it after the window\r\n REQ: When a declared blackout window is armed, the delivered coordination and unattended operation shall pause new model work until the window ends, preserving each claimed lane at its committed pause point and starting no model work inside the window except an adjudication needed to bring an active lane to that point, then resume eligible work after the window without retaining a session whose prior use predates that window's end.\r\n AC: At a window boundary the end is exclusive, a wrapping interval belongs to its weekday start, and a changed declaration applies on the next reading. A new ordinary call or claim is refused during the interval; an adjudication for an active claimed work item may run to its pause point; the loop waits and retries after the interval; and the first retained keep after the interval retires a record last used before its end while a use at or after the end remains eligible to resume.\r\n status Approved\r\n\r\nSR-032 Onboarding and dev-setup scaffold\r\n REQ: The onboarding and dev-setup templates shall scaffold and run to a green developer setup.\r\n AC: The scaffolded onboard/dev-setup scripts run to a green setup. When this repository's Windows developer setup has no interpreter at the runtime floor, its attended install operation offers one consent-first through an available provisioner, searches again after either response, and otherwise exits with the installation step; declining runs no provisioner.\r\n status Approved","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"3914207c-7f30-4d10-b71e-bf15c1758fe7","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:16:21.089Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"?? docs/reviews/wi-927/005-ADJUDICATE-65a3405.md\n?? docs/reviews/wi-927/005-ADJUDICATE-65a3405.md.requested\n65a340522 WI-927: the checkpoint's reconcile: LLR-322, LLR-300 and TC-345 state the settled fix; the Trust section reads the ratchet line and corrects the offer's count; decision D-010\n4b20a7bc3 WI-927: the round-2 MINOR fix: a failed install names its fix, a NUL stdin is no terminal on Windows, and the PowerShell offers print the guard's text; LLR-322's back-links; decision D-009\n0c41237c9 WI-927: counted round 2, filed (Sol CHANGES-REQUESTED 1 MINOR; Opus CHANGES-REQUESTED 5 MINOR); decision D-008\n9bbcfb351 WI-927: fix round 1: a JSON null reads occupied, the consent question shows at a POSIX terminal, and the pseudo-terminal tests answer no; decision D-007\nbrief = combined\nkinds = amendment\noutcome = pending\n124:human_approval_through = \"DevStg-Boundary\"\nSR-229 Coordinator claim admission respects a blackout pause\r\n REQ: Where a blackout window is armed, the delivered work-item admission shall refuse a new claim inside that window on every route at any context-guard dial; outside a