{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQ8X61LcyLngv5pU1cJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've committed the WI-927 verdict as `6a1c89bb3` with the `WI: WI-927` trailer, and the commit checks passed. Its machine lines are `VERDICT: MEANING rows=3` and `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment`, and I took no act.\n\nI checked the file with the kit's own readers. The sitting parser accepts it under the combined binding, and `blessed_rows` returns exactly LLR-300, LLR-322 and TC-345, so the later act turn re-attests all three.\n\n**What changed** (all MEANING):\n- **LLR-322:** the old merge, which replaced only the guard's own commands inside shared hook groups, is gone. The guard hooks are now read by name into one of four states:\n  - **none:** the example declares no guard hooks.\n  - **absent:** a terminal \"yes\" installs them, from dev-setup or the lease take.\n  - **on:** nothing to do.\n  - **occupied:** something else holds the slot, so nothing is written and the file, events and fix are named.\n\n  A failed read is reported as missing, never as none.\n- **LLR-300:** the lease take now records no holder unless the hooks read none or on, or a consented install succeeds.\n- **TC-345:** verifies both rows, and all 33 cited tests exist.\n\n**Why all three are tagged `[MEANING+BLESS]`:**\n- **The owner made both calls.** D-011 found command-level ownership contrived; D-019 made the lease take a first-run install route that keeps the consent step.\n- **The rule is closed and fails safe.** It has four states, and an occupied slot writes nothing.\n- **The take gate serves both parents.** The holder only gets the drain and blackout close-down instructions through these hooks, which is what SR-229 and SR-237 require.\n- **One home for the rule.** LLR-300 states only the take's gate and leaves the state rules to LLR-322.\n\n**On SR-229, I took reading (b):** its list doesn't cover every lease-take condition, so SR-229 stays as approved.\n- **Where the clause sits:** \"a subsequent session may take the freed lease\" closes the hand-back sentence. It says the hand-back frees the lease; it doesn't list the take's preconditions.\n- **The take already has an unlisted refusal.** It refuses when another holder exists, a rule that lives only in LLR-300.\n- **The new condition is design detail.** The hooks precondition belongs one tier down, and a session that consents can still take the lease.\n\n**Two advisories, neither blocking:**\n1. **Vague wording:** \"No re-enable path exists\" in LLR-322 doesn't say which act is gone. It could say plainly that the consent offer at \"absent\" is the only install route.\n2. **TC-345's tier** reads `Smoke` while it cites two modules that only run in the full suite, so it should read `Full`.\n\nThe untracked `005-ADJUDICATE-65a3405.md.requested` is the coordinator's, and I didn't touch it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3538,"cache_read_input_tokens":903595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3538},"output_tokens":734,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"c9afab86-cf04-4af2-abf4-7ab955c90a89","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:18:45.584Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQ8WS4vdw9qMnJtMhJd"}
